# Prevents SecSettings from offering/checking for stock Samsung OTA updates,
# since ReCoreUI doesn't ship a stock OTA client (ChoiDujour.apk).
#
# Ported from UN1CA's customize.sh, which only applied this when
# system/priv-app/ChoiDujour/ChoiDujour.apk was absent from the build. That
# guard was dropped here since ReCoreUI does not bundle ChoiDujour - if that
# ever changes, wrap this file's application in a check for it instead of
# applying it unconditionally.
#
# NOTE: isOTAUpgradeAllowed(Landroid/content/Context;)Z is assumed to be a
# `public static` method (register p0 = the Context parameter, reused to hold
# the boolean return value, per UN1CA's own SMALI_PATCH "return" convention).
# Verify against your decompiled baseline; if it's an instance method instead,
# change `.locals 0` / `p0` to whatever register your build's method actually
# uses for its boolean result.

FILE smali_classes3/com/samsung/android/settings/softwareupdate/SoftwareUpdateUtils.smali
REPLACE .method public static isOTAUpgradeAllowed(Landroid/content/Context;)Z
    .locals 0

    const/4 p0, 0x0

    return p0
END

END
